say good morning happy New Year to Kurt  Warner Kurt thanks for joining us how  are you good you as well thank you the  best coaching vacancy is where well  that's a great question I think the  bottom line is you always want to have a  quarterback and so you need look at  different spots I mean Derek Carr I  think there's a great situation there  with some some talent they were a team  that was successful a couple years ago  the harder argue with with Detroit I  think they got a lot of young pieces  some good playmakers on offense and a  quarterback as well so when I look at it  I look at the quarterback spot and those  are a couple guys that are established  anyways but some good young quarterbacks  and some other places as well yeah the  Andrew Luck situation so we don't know  if that's a good job or not because  exactly why is that such a mystery what  happened with Andrew Luck well I mean I  don't know if it's so much a mystery is  you know you're never quite sure how  people bounce back from certain injuries  and specifically when you're talking  about the right arm and you know I don't  know if it was mismanaged or it just  hasn't bounced back like they had  thought but but yeah I think anybody's  got to be a little bit leery and scary  of that scared of that situation because  man I just can't believe that it's taken  this long for him to be able to to get  back on the field you know and that's  even in practice throwing it around and  doing what you expected to do and you  know me personally not in any  information on the situation but I'm  wondering if he's going to be able to to  really come back and play at this point  yeah how important is this next game for  Blake bortles future in Jacksonville I  think it's extremely important I mean I  think they've had a great year I think  they have all the pieces there to say  man we can we can do this for a while  but it all comes down to that  quarterback position and he's got to  prove that he can consistently play at  that level and win games in the playoffs  I mean you don't want to continue to  move forward if you believe you got a  running game and a defense but not that  guy that can pull it  and win those games for you so I think  it's it's vital how he plays in the next  game or two and if he shows he can  actually win games against good teams  and good quarterbacks on the other side  yeah it's just a mystery there that he  had that run where he had seven  touchdowns no picks and then everybody  was back on board then these last couple  of games you just can't have that if  you're gonna be a consistent team  elsewhere you can't have that in an  inconsistency and it feels like he's  playing for his job every game now from  now on out in Jacksonville yeah well I  mean and you mentioned it it's all about  consistency can I expect that position  to show up weekend and week out and go  head to head with another good  quarterback if need be but not make the  mistakes that can cost our football team  and you know you continue you know like  you said he had that run and you go okay  maybe he can you know turn the corner  but in the back of everybody's mind is  still the Blake bortles that we saw  early in his career and then we've seen  it the last couple games and you know  the organization has to continue to say  you know we don't want to go into a game  wondering if that guy's going to come  out and so I think it's very important  against playoff teams to show that he  can make some plays to help them win not  just be a guy that can stand back there  and not make the mistakes to lose the  game for me can you assess a college  quarterback and have any like can you  handicap that at all playing at a high  level and being a hall-of-famer if  you're looking at these guys Baker  Mayfield or Josh Allen or Sam D'Arnot or  Josh Rosen can you look for one thing  and say that they're gonna be good in  the NFL absolutely not a couple factors  here I mean you know there's such  discrepancy at times between the college  talent for one team compared to another  team and I tweeted earlier this year  when I watched Oklahoma play it looked  like everybody was wide open you know me  and that's just not gonna happen at the  next level the guys aren't going to be  run  free wide-open you've got the spread  systems that aren't really based on  reading defenses and coverages and  having to get the ball to the right  place on time and so you don't know how  they're gonna translate there and then  the hardest thing is always the mental  part of it is I've seen quarterbacks  that were great college quarterbacks  that get to the NFL and they just can't  make those strides to get better and  better every year and then you see other  guys and you know Tom Brady is always a  great example that gets you know average  college career gets picked late in the  draft yet every year it seems like he  gets better and better and better and  you never know that until a guy gets  into that environment in that situation  and you push him and you know you give  him more and more and he plays against  the best talent and you can see that and  I think that's why it's so hard to gauge  that position and who's going to be good  and who's not because they can be great  right now but you need a guy to be even  better two years from now and even  better than that four years from now and  nobody can really gauge whether whether  a player can do that or not what  Mayfield's personality scare you or it  tracked you to him oh yeah I don't think  it would scare me away you know I think  you would have to sit down and talk to  him and you know some of the other parts  that go with the personality I'm and I  love the energy I love what you know he  brings to the table from that standpoint  I heard somebody kind of compare them to  a Brett Favre and there's those aspects  that you really love well I think  there's a there's points you got to tone  it down a little bit and still be able  to be the the face of a franchise but I  think that's about conversations and  about talking to a young kid and  figuring out whether he can mature and  develop and and understand the two sides  of that coin I'll leave you with this  there was a report Josh Rosen said that  he didn't want to be drafted by  Cleveland what do you make of that what  I make is you know on the surface you  completely understand that side of  things and go man I want to go somewhere  where I believe I can be successful and  there's a  organization hasn't for a long time but  to me the other side of it is I want to  go to Cleveland and I want to change  things if I can go to Cleveland and turn  that organization around I've done  something extremely special and  something memorable and that's how I  would look at it as a competitor but you  fully understand the other side and want  to make sure you have a chance to  succeed and they're going to give you  time and excuse me and they're gonna  keep the coach there for a period of  time and allow you to build something  and they haven't done that very well in  Cleveland so you understand the  trepidation that a guy would have in  going there and really believing they're  going to have a chance to to be a great  one current we appreciate your time good  luck this weekend  sounds good we'll talk to you soon  that's Kurt Warner and I fell Network  analyst they got games on Saturday and  Sunday and started noon eastern on  Saturday and 7:00 a.m. Eastern on Sunday  for more Dan Patrick show to the  audience channel 239 on Direct TV or  download the Dan Patrick show app  [Music]

